  "Comments": "<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;font-size:12pt\"><DIV><DIV><DIV><P><SPAN>The Australian Hydrological Geospatial Fabric (Geofabric) is a specialised Geographic Information System (GIS). It registers the spatial relationships between important hydrological features such as rivers, catchments, water bodies, aquifers and monitoring points. The enduring nature of the Geofabric is based on a set of contracted nodes (points) which represent important hydrological features in the landscape.<\/SPAN><\/P><P><SPAN>A subset of the contracted nodes is used to create a simplified node-link network with associated contracted catchments. There is also a hierarchy of catchments, as well as alternate representations to meet varied user requirements.<\/SPAN><\/P><\/DIV><\/DIV><\/DIV><\/DIV>",
